  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt strict incident reporting, a 55 °C / 5% thermal test limit with regulator-approved corrective action and exact customer-facing test rates but no public per-model rates, a 6-year retrofit deadline, built-in suppression at 36 months, and a mandatory 8 per 100,000 recall trigger with prompt customer notices. The deal satisfies both sides' red lines: no public per-model failure rates for Northwind, exact customer test results for Halcyon, a 6-year retrofit window, and a 36-month suppression deadline."
